From 408ac1ec632ac2db47e8e1f3e85306dd0f39f7b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:45:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Aurora: every in-between frame gets the HD look, not only
 the first

The HD look's effects (ambient occlusion, sun and cloud shadows, edge and
torch light, far blur, bloom) run once a frame, keyed by the frame and
whether it is an in-between one. Smooth Motion draws three in-between
frames a game frame at 120 FPS, five at 180 and seven at 240, all with the
same key, so only the first got the effects: the frames went with and
without them in turn, and clouds, glow and shadows flickered above 60 FPS.
The key now includes the in-between frame's step.
---
 GXRuntime/graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/common.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/GXRuntime/graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/common.cpp b/GXRuntime/graphics/aurora/lib/gfx/common.cpp
